BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 485.4 Td (- The world is a five-by-five grid with one object. The comparison is with an attribution that takes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 472.2 Td (every change for its own doing, which is easy to beat.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 452.2 Td (- The simulated engine does not think: it echoes, and accepts or dismisses by a fixed rule. Behaviour) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 439.1 Td (here depends only on the mechanisms of the loop.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 419.1 Td (- Histories differ by the outcome attached to each sentence by the experimenter; this is a manipulation) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 406.0 Td (of inputs, not a lived experience.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 386.0 Td (- The behaviour vector is coarse \(shares of sources, rates of acceptance, speech, memory and recall\); a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 372.9 Td (real difference could escape it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 352.9 Td (- Few independent units: intervals are wide. Many comparisons: some will look notable by chance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 332.9 Td (- With a remote engine the results would not be reproducible, since such models change.) Tj ET
